(3) and since he was a firstborn, he takes two shares.

original_row.English:
The law is one and the same for the son and the daughter in inheritance,
except that the son takes a double portion from the property of the father,
but he does not take a double portion from the property of the mother;
and daughters are maintained from the father’s property;
but they are not maintained from the mother’s property.

